{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1015274-secrets-of-the-covenants-not-a-member-merits","id":1015274,"title":"Secrets of the Covenants: Not a member Merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-10T09:46:18-08:00","id":1015274,"title":"Secrets of the Covenants: Not a member Merits","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> So we have the 5 merits, one for each covenant, where they grant some benefits. In some cases, it feels like the majority of the covenant members would actually just have these merits and no status (looking mostly at Chorister and Laity merits), but even others feel like something like a stepping stone. For example, someone who wants to join the Invictus first takes One Foot in the Door, and then once he finds whom to swear an Oath to him, then he moves to having a status and someone sworn to him (since to be Invictus, you need to be a part of at least one Oath).<br /> <br /> This has some big implications for the setting, and as far as I know, that's the intent. But...<br /> <br /> It feels like the Majority of members would go through this stage, then why does this have the benefit of granting two dots of Covenant Status, should someone join it? If you were a Chorister or a Member of Laity for years, and then decide to become a priest for the faith or greater duties, why would you get two dots of Status?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T09:57:01-08:00","id":1015278,"title":"","content":"Because you've been a well-regarded friend of the covenant for years.<br /> <br /> I don't feel that the majority of members go through that stage, most likely stick to their covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T10:39:48-08:00","id":1015299,"title":"","content":"That's a very... out of character way of looking at things. If my concept involves being the scion of an Invictus House, I'm not going to start off with an association merit, I'm going to jump right into Status 1. Because I would not be an associate, I'd be a full member. If I have a concept that revolves around being a LeS priest with a congression of nomadic vampires, it makes no sense to have a merit that revolves around being part of the laity.<br /> <br /> There's a million character concepts where going through a not-member status doesn't make sense at all While it seem to make sense if you come at the covenants from a blank slate, but in the messy political environment of the All Night Society, that's not a given. There's peer pressure, biological needs, lies and misdirections all around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-10-2016, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T10:53:39-08:00","id":1015306,"title":"","content":"I would argue that the Covenant Pledge Merits are like an alternative to Status 1. Some Sanctified join the Clergy right away, others join the Deaconry first. Those who start out as Ministers might move on to become Pastors, while those who start out as Deacons may be chosen to become Vicars for the local Bishop, maybe even Legates. Some Invictus apply for an entry-level position and work their way up the corporate ladder, others start out as interns and develop a good relationship with the company management so they can get a better starting job when their internship is over. It's like an alternate advancement track.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T12:34:29-08:00","id":1015336,"title":"","content":"I disagree about it being a very &quot;out of character way of looking at things.&quot;. Yes, there's a shit ton of concepts where it makes no sense to be at that level. But most characters (and that means that for most of those concepts the past themselves) had this merit.<br /> <br /> Almost no Circle member becomes a priest immediately, most of them would first join a Chorus, and then move up. Similarly, someone who's wanting to join Invictus, will most likely first make friends there (unless he has some sire/mentor or someone who can get him the status immediately).<br /> <br /> Sure, I totally agree that there are several paths into it. But why make it the rule of the merit that you get immediately to two? That's what I'm struggling with. Most of these not-a-member who join fully, wouldn't be any higher than someone who had a respectable sire put them into the covenant immediately upon embrace.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T18:07:31-08:00","id":1015434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1015274-secrets-of-the-covenants-not-a-member-merits?p=1015336#post1015336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, I totally agree that there are several paths into it. But why make it the rule of the merit that you get immediately to two? That's what I'm struggling with. Most of these not-a-member who join fully, wouldn't be any higher than someone who had a respectable sire put them into the covenant immediately upon embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>In world, because as you pointed out a member who has been an ally and known the covenant is not going to have to start out as a basic apprentice because their loyalty has already been proven.<br /> <br /> Out of world, because it's a 2-dot Merit and so worth 2 dots of Status.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T18:44:02-08:00","id":1015462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1015274-secrets-of-the-covenants-not-a-member-merits?p=1015336#post1015336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But most characters (and that means that for most of those concepts the past themselves) had this merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree that most Covenant members would have started as Pledges. Like, I'm sure a lot do, but not most. And even if most do, I don't think it really matters, as there will always be some that buck the trend, and for those people, it's important that Status 1 exists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1015274-secrets-of-the-covenants-not-a-member-merits?p=1015336#post1015336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost no Circle member becomes a priest immediately, most of them would first join a Chorus, and then move up. Similarly, someone who's wanting to join Invictus, will most likely first make friends there (unless he has some sire/mentor or someone who can get him the status immediately).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree in the specific case of Circle of the Crone (of course, appropriately, their Pledge Merit gives access to Covenant Merits, which makes it even more appealing than the others to someone considering joining). But I'm sure there are plenty of Invictus with Sires that get them entry-level positions right away. I imagine there are at least as many Carthians who start out getting directly involved in the revolution as there are fence-sitters who want to attend some meetings before going full rebel alliance. The Ordo Dracul has access to resources, research, mentors, peer review, etc., seems to me like it would be more appealing for those interested in transcending the Kindred Condition to join them straight off than to struggle with independent study first. The Sanctified are probably in a similar boat to the Circle that there probably aren't a ton of them that start out as priests without spending at least a little time in the Laity, but there are always the rare exceptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1015274-secrets-of-the-covenants-not-a-member-merits?p=1015336#post1015336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, I totally agree that there are several paths into it. But why make it the rule of the merit that you get immediately to two? That's what I'm struggling with. Most of these not-a-member who join fully, wouldn't be any higher than someone who had a respectable sire put them into the covenant immediately upon embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Nofather said, the Doylist answer is cause the Pledge Merits cost two dots, and you lose it when you join the Covenant properly, so giving them two dots of Status ensures you don't have to lose a dot worth of benefits and replace it under Sanctity of Merits. The Wattsonian answer is that a Pledge is already the equivalent of an entry-level member, they're just coming at it another way. The new guy with One Foot In The Door and the guy who was Embraced into the Covenant are held to the same degree of importance, and if either of them moves up, they move up to the same next step.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T18:56:57-08:00","id":1015470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1015274-secrets-of-the-covenants-not-a-member-merits?p=1015336#post1015336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree about it being a very &amp;quot;out of character way of looking at things.&amp;quot;. Yes, there's a shit ton of concepts where it makes no sense to be at that level. But most characters (and that means that for most of those concepts the past themselves) had this merit.<br /> <br /> Almost no Circle member becomes a priest immediately, most of them would first join a Chorus, and then move up. Similarly, someone who's wanting to join Invictus, will most likely first make friends there (unless he has some sire/mentor or someone who can get him the status immediately).<br /> <br /> Sure, I totally agree that there are several paths into it. But why make it the rule of the merit that you get immediately to two? That's what I'm struggling with. Most of these not-a-member who join fully, wouldn't be any higher than someone who had a respectable sire put them into the covenant immediately upon embrace.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't take this as me supporting the concept of the pseudo-status merits (I don't.) but merits are a game mechanic that frequently give the players insurance to bypass roleplaying out the cause and effect of their action or inactions by saying they maintain their alliances between scenes, practice at the shooting range or boxing club to justify their 5 brawl/5 firearms and attendant merits even if they don't do a single thing in game to ensure their skill is up to par or they haven't inadvertently pissed off an ally or what have you. This merit simply lets players reap the benefits of covenant membership and fast track their admission without eating up game time actually trying to ingratiate themselves with the covenant in question. Alternatively, it lets players farm the covenant specific benefits right at the start of the game more easily than actually dedicating game time to join the covenant that has them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T04:45:32-08:00","id":1015640,"title":"","content":"I think you're just misunderstanding what the merits are intended for, Griautis. You seem to be treating them as the gateway into the covenants for all members to pass through. If that was true, then I don't think that each merit would say some variation of &quot;If your character joins&quot; and &quot;greater than an average newbie.&quot; A qualifier and a clear statement that this merit is the exception, not the rule, for when it comes to joining a covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T06:45:56-08:00","id":1015660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1015274-secrets-of-the-covenants-not-a-member-merits?p=1015640#post1015640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're just misunderstanding what the merits are intended for, Griautis. You seem to be treating them as the gateway into the covenants for all members to pass through. If that was true, then I don't think that each merit would say some variation of &quot;If your character joins&quot; and &quot;greater than an average newbie.&quot; A qualifier and a clear statement that this merit is the exception, not the rule, for when it comes to joining a covenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'll gladly buy that for most of the Covenants. Chorister however, is totally different in that regard. You get the sorcery, the merits, everything and more a starter needs, and your title (Chorister) correspond to what most likely most Circle of the Crone members are (just part of some Chorus). With lesser extent similar things could be said of Carthian and Lancea merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T09:27:24-08:00","id":1015699,"title":"","content":"*Shrugs* If you want to run things that way, more power to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T08:07:14-08:00","id":1016554,"title":"","content":"They're also good ways to show an alliance between two covenants in a city.<br /> <br /> Maybe a city is ruled by Invictus, which one joins if one wants a civic position or power, but the vampires the city are religious, the Local Invictus are close to the Lancea Sanctum, so much of the Invictus there have Laity merit, and only Priests and the most devote join Lancea Santum directly, kind of like the midevil fuedal system.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Ordo Dracul and say CoC have a common occult interest in something that they can't do alone, but various member take their not a member merit in the other covenant to better tie them together. <br /> <br /> Just a couple of examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:08:28-08:00","id":1016816,"title":"","content":"I think someone already pointed it out in another thread but. Thematically The power of Cruac comes from the beast through the lens of pagan traditions. So to the circle the power comes from the beast, so it isn't so much learned magic, but more of releasing the power already in the blood. Their stance is that everyone already has Cruac inside them, just waiting to be unlocked. At the cost of humanity cap. So they're more willing to give a taste of Cruac to see if you'll slide further down the slope.<br /> <br /> And I do believe changeling had a simular system with its Friend of the Court Merits<br /> <br /> That may not answer the direct question, but hopefully more context can be presented","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T23:39:00-08:00","id":1016928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1015274-secrets-of-the-covenants-not-a-member-merits?p=1016816#post1016816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think someone already pointed it out in another thread but. Thematically The power of Cruac comes from the beast through the lens of pagan traditions. So to the circle the power comes from the beast, so it isn't so much learned magic, but more of releasing the power already in the blood. Their stance is that everyone already has Cruac inside them, just waiting to be unlocked. At the cost of humanity cap. So they're more willing to give a taste of Cruac to see if you'll slide further down the slope.<br /> <br /> And I do believe changeling had a simular system with its Friend of the Court Merits<br /> <br /> That may not answer the direct question, but hopefully more context can be presented</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see where that belief comes from... Sources?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T00:55:46-08:00","id":1016936,"title":"","content":"Having the exact answer to the world's metaphysics and the belief of every single crone is a little beyond prophetic. Read up on some homework, 1ed Circle of Crone Book. Innate Properties page 33","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T05:33:27-08:00","id":1016998,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Ritual Discipline taught by the Circle of the Crone, Cr\u00faac is an ancient, malevolent art \u2014 described by some opponents of the covenant as a <i><b>literal infection of Vitae, a thing living within its practitioners</b></i>. The power summoned by Cr\u00faac rites is <i><b>the power of the Beast itself,</b></i> paid in blood and forced to taint the world by invoking the primal gods of the Crone.&quot; 2e Requiem core, page 150, emphasis mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T23:22:46-08:00","id":1017511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1015274-secrets-of-the-covenants-not-a-member-merits?p=1016816#post1016816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think someone already pointed it out in another thread but. Thematically The power of Cruac comes from the beast through the lens of pagan traditions. So to the circle the power comes from the beast, so it isn't so much learned magic, but more of releasing the power already in the blood. Their stance is that everyone already has Cruac inside them, just waiting to be unlocked. At the cost of humanity cap. So they're more willing to give a taste of Cruac to see if you'll slide further down the slope.<br /> <br /> And I do believe changeling had a simular system with its Friend of the Court Merits<br /> <br /> That may not answer the direct question, but hopefully more context can be presented</div> </div> </div> </div> Courtgood Will is the merit for Changeling and yeah, this is the vampire equivalant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T23:37:01-08:00","id":1017517,"title":"","content":"I'd generally assume that someone embraced into a Covenant (their Sire is a member and it's the part of Kindred society they enter through) starts at Status 1, while someone who comes in from the outside as Kindred via having to build those connections does so through the &quot;Not a Member&quot; Merit.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you can just assume that the &quot;Not a Member&quot; merits are specifically for members of other Covenants - hence the distinction between it an Status 1","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"